  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Strengthening good governance and education through digitalisation for economic transformation of Bhutan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Action will build on and consolidate the budget support programme on &#xbf;Good Governance and Digitalisation&#xbf; (AAP 2022) under priority 2 and 3 of the MIP 2021-2027. The proposed action will support digitalisation in two complementary sectors: 1) education (from pre-school to secondary, including TVET schools) and 2) finance (for public service delivery and enhanced fiscal responsibility). It aims to support Bhutan&#xbf;s 21st century economic roadmap and Bhutan&#xbf;s national Digital Strategy. It is aligned to the sectoral National Education Policy and the PFM reform strategy, as well as with the Bhutan&#xbf;s National Digital and AI Strategies to harness digital technologies for stimulating economic growth, improving productivity, and generate quality jobs.</narrative>
  </description>
